<% content_for :own_heading, true %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
  <%= render "admin/component_demo/environment_banner" %>

  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <% description = "Changing a quarter's teaching days changes what its unfinalized grade books will " \
                   "pay. Four ways to say so, and which to build." %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "School day impact", description: description } do %><% end %>

  <div class="space-y-10">
    <section data-testid="impact-today">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Today</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
        The field says nothing. Real exposure on <%= @school_year&.name || "this database" %>:
      </p>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <dl class="space-y-1 text-sm">
          <% @exposure.each do |quarter, counts| %>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
              <dt class="text-slate-700"><%= quarter.name %>
                <span class="text-slate-500">&middot; <%= quarter.school_days || "not set" %> days</span>
              </dt>
              <dd class="tabular-nums text-slate-900">
                <%= counts[:books].zero? ? "nothing depends on it" : "#{pluralize(counts[:entries], 'entry')} in #{pluralize(counts[:books], 'open grade book')}" %>
              </dd>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </dl>
      <% end %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
        Note the shape of it: three quarters carry exposure and one carries none, and a second school year
        carries none at all. Whatever is built has to be <strong>silent when there is nothing to say</strong> -
        a notice on every quarter of every school year is one nobody reads by the third visit.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="impact-option-a">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">A. A hint on the field &mdash; recommended</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
        In the hint slot the form builder already renders, under the label and above the input, on the
        quarters that have exposure and no others.
      </p>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <p class="tw-label-primary">Quarter 1</p>
            <p class="tw-field-hint mb-2">2 entries in 1 open grade book use this.</p>
            <div class="tw-input-primary flex items-center text-slate-500">44</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="tw-label-primary">Quarter 4</p>
            <p class="tw-field-hint mb-2">Nothing depends on this yet.</p>
            <div class="tw-input-primary flex items-center text-slate-500">47</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
        It is attached to the thing it describes, which a page-level callout is not, and it is legible
        before anybody types. It states the blast radius rather than a delta, because the delta depends on
        a number that does not exist until it is typed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="impact-option-b">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">B. A callout above the form</h2>
      <%= render "components/ui/callout",
                 tone: :warning,
                 title: "Two quarters here feed grade books that are not finalized",
                 body: "Changing their teaching days changes what those books will pay." %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <strong>Rejected.</strong> It says the same thing as A, one level further from the field, and it
        cannot say <em>which</em> without listing the quarters back to you - at which point it is A with
        extra steps. A callout earns a page when the message is about the page; this one is about four
        specific inputs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="impact-option-c">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">C. The exact delta, in the confirmation &mdash; recommended</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
        On submit, when a value actually changed and something depends on it. The app's own dialog, and the
        figure computed by <code>EarningsCalculator</code> - the same object that pays.
      </p>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">Change teaching days?</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
          Quarter 1 goes from 44 days to 46. That changes perfect attendance for 2 students in 1 grade
          book, which is $2.00 less when it is finalized.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700">
          Nothing is paid until a teacher finalizes, and you can change this back.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <span class="tw-btn-primary">Change teaching days</span>
          <span class="tw-btn-secondary">Cancel</span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
        This is the one that carries information A cannot: the direction and the amount. It states that
        nothing is paid yet and that the change is reversible, because a dialog that only says "are you
        sure" makes a reversible action feel irreversible.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="impact-option-d">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">D. Tell them afterwards, in the flash</h2>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
          "School year updated. 2 students in 1 grade book now earn $1.00 less each."
        </p>
      <% end %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <strong>Rejected as the only measure, kept as a fallback.</strong> The flash auto-dismisses after
        six seconds, so it is the wrong place for the one sentence somebody may need to act on - and this
        app's own rule is that a message which removes itself must be an outcome rather than a state. As a
        confirmation of what just happened it is fine; as the only warning it is a message you can miss by
        looking away.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="impact-recommendation">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Recommendation: A and C</h2>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
          <strong>A</strong> is standing context, on the field, before you type: <em>something depends on
          this</em>. <strong>C</strong> is the specific consequence at the moment you commit: <em>this much,
          in this direction</em>. They are not two statements of one fact - one is exposure and the other
          is a delta - and each is silent when there is nothing to say.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">
          What I would not build is a live recalculation as you type. It is the most satisfying version and
          the least honest: it needs an endpoint, a Stimulus controller and a debounce, and it puts a money
          figure on screen for a value nobody has committed to. The confirmation already arrives at the
          only moment the number is real.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">
          One thing worth stating in the copy either way: <strong>this is reversible</strong>. Nothing is
          paid until a teacher finalizes, and the finalize dialog states its own total. design.md's rule
          about showing what an irreversible action will do does not strictly apply here - which is exactly
          why the dialog should say so rather than imply otherwise.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
